    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d817">

                <pb facs="0995" n="977" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg977"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/6–1946</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/> No. 50</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-07-08">July 8, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Receipt is acknowledged of your despatch
                    no. 18 of June 19, 1946,<anchor n="12" xml:id="d817-f1"/> regarding the
                    conversation you had with Dr. Ezequiel Padilla and his request that you speak to
                    President Avila Camacho, expressing the interest of the United States in free
                    and fair elections in Mexico.</p>
                <p>The Department approves of your reply to Dr. Padilla to the effect that you could
                    not take the action he requested. However, if in private conversation the
                    President should make reference to his remarks regarding the election, you are
                    authorized, in your discretion, to express to him this Government’s continuing
                    interest and hope that the authority of all governments be derived from the will
                    of the majority of the people through regularly and freely expressed fair and
                    democratic processes.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Acting Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Spruille Braden</hi></signed></closer>
                <pb facs="0996" n="978" xml:id="pg978"/>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[Miguel Alemán was elected President of Mexico on July 7 for a 6-year period
                        beginning December 1, 1946.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
